version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
url: "https://github.com/rxp613-dev/contrastive-dta"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23308152"
abstract: |
  Complete reproducibility package for our systematic empirical benchmark of contrastive
  learning (CL) for drug-target affinity (DTA) prediction. This v1.1.0 release includes
  the V9 convergent-protocol (Config C) reassessment: the original apparent gains
  (+26% to +62%) were shown to reflect CL stabilizing a prematurely stopped baseline
  rather than genuine improvement; under the convergent protocol, CL does not produce
  net gain and may even harm cold-target generalization. Includes 300+ training runs,
  115-directory audit with config-level verification, Holm-corrected statistical analysis,
  and comprehensive supplementary materials (S1–S8).
